  "conventions": {
    "frame_size": "<integer>",
    "statistics": "median and interquartile range over active frames, quantiles by linear interpolation at q (n - 1) between the sorted values; a frame is active when its RMS lies within 40 dB of the loudest frame",
    "spectral": "magnitude weights for shape, power for band shares; periodic Hann frames of frame_size samples, hop frame_size / 4, centred and zero-padded; frame_size is 8192 when the note list has a median f0 below 100 Hz, else 4096, and 4096 without a note list",
    "bpm": "the tempo of the beat grid and of every later step: bpm_refined when its confidence is high, else bpm_given",
    "bpm_given": "given by --bpm",
    "bpm_refined": "onset strength: the rise of each third-octave band power from 30 Hz, compressed as ln(1 + P / knee) with the knee 60 dB below full scale, against the frame 10 ms earlier, in 46.4 ms Hann frames on a 1 ms hop, low-passed at 20 Hz, less its 100 ms mean, below 10 % of its largest rise set to 0; each tempo t with |given / t - 1| at most 3 % (2.91 % below to 3.09 % above the given one), in 0.01 BPM steps, scores the unbiased autocorrelation summed at 1 to 32 beats; the refined tempo is used when its score is at least 1.5 times the median score (tempo_peak) and either 0.4 of the lag count times the zero-lag autocorrelation (beat_periodicity), or 0.75 of that on every second or fourth beat lag alone (sparse_periodicity) with at most 0.8 peaks of the onset strength per beat (onsets_per_beat), and at least 0.9 of the energy of the rise before its low-pass lies within 25 ms of its peaks, each the largest within 30 ms (onset_sharpness); both shares stop at 1; cycles_in_span counts the whole beats of the stem",
    "duration_s": "decoded frames over the sample rate",
    "sample_rate_hz": "the native rate of the file; no resampling",
    "band_edge_hz": "long-term power spectrum of the mid over the active frames that lie wholly inside the stem, median-smoothed over one semitone on each side; where the smoothed level falls at least 25 dB over one semitone above 2 kHz and the median level of the octave below lies within 20 dB of the level where the fall starts, the edge is the half-depth point of the steepest such fall; otherwise the noise floor is the lowest level above 1 kHz and the edge is the highest bin at least 30 dB above it, at low confidence, or the Nyquist frequency when no bin above 1 kHz is",
    "hard_limited": "true when runs of at least 1 ms of samples within 1e-5 of the channel peak, each with its neighbours on both sides at least half the peak on the same side, cover at least 0.1 % of a channel",
    "peak_dbfs": "peak and RMS of the mono mix over the whole stem in dB relative to full scale 1.0; a full-scale sine reads -3.01 dB RMS; crest is peak minus RMS",
    "rms_dbfs": "peak and RMS of the mono mix over the whole stem in dB relative to full scale 1.0; a full-scale sine reads -3.01 dB RMS; crest is peak minus RMS",
    "crest_db": "peak and RMS of the mono mix over the whole stem in dB relative to full scale 1.0; a full-scale sine reads -3.01 dB RMS; crest is peak minus RMS",
    "centroid_hz": "magnitude weights |X_k| divided by the window sum, periodic Hann frames, statistics over active frames as median and interquartile range",
    "centroid_over_f0": "the centroid of each active frame over the median f0 of the note list, MIDI pitch to hertz with A4 = 440 Hz; null without a note list",
    "spread_hz": "magnitude weights |X_k| divided by the window sum, periodic Hann frames, statistics over active frames as median and interquartile range",
    "rolloff85_hz": "magnitude weights |X_k| divided by the window sum, periodic Hann frames, statistics over active frames as median and interquartile range",
    "rolloff95_hz": "magnitude weights |X_k| divided by the window sum, periodic Hann frames, statistics over active frames as median and interquartile range",
    "flatness": "geometric over arithmetic mean of the magnitude, floored at 1e-5 after the window-sum scale, bins from 100 Hz to 10 kHz",
    "band_share": "power |X_k|^2 summed over active frames per band, divided by the power in the bands reported; bands start at 20, 60, 250, 1000, 4000 and 10000 Hz and end at the next start or 20 kHz; a band that starts at or above the Nyquist frequency is left out, and one that crosses it ends there",
    "stereo": "rho: Pearson correlation at zero lag; sm_db: 20 log10(rms(S) / rms(M)) with M = (L + R) / 2 and S = (L - R) / 2; per band from the 8192-point Hann STFT over bins inside the band, DC excluded; ipd_deg: abs(angle(L conj R)) at the largest cross-spectrum bin within 2 bins of h f0, h = 1..20 inside the band, weighted by |L conj R|, then the mean over active frames, whose RMS over both channels, sqrt((rms_L^2 + rms_R^2) / 2), lies within 40 dB of the loudest; bands: sub below 120 Hz, low_mid 120 Hz to 1 kHz, high above 1 kHz",
    "confidence": "level, reasons and spread of each estimate; the spread of a statistic is its interquartile range and that of the band edge one bin width, in the unit of the value; estimate false means no value, with the reasons why",
    "pitch": "the pitch layer of a monophonic line, read from the f0 track, the note list and the sub-band line; values is null when the line plays chords or has no notes; every time is audio time from the start of the stem",
    "glides": "pitch in cents of the voiced f0 frames; a stable pitch is a span of 50 ms or more within 30 cents of its running mean whose least-squares slope stays at 86 cents per second or less; a glide joins two stable pitches 100 cents or more apart that match notes of different pitch within 50 cents, where the slope of the 5-frame moving average stays at 86 cents per second or more, in the direction of the motion, over 90 ms or more; s(x) = 1 - (1 - x)^p is fitted between the two stable pitches by least squares over the motion and 50 ms of each; start_s is the fitted start less the track's lag of a quarter frame, 23.2 ms, less half a period; time_s is the full 0 to 100 % time; from_silence marks a glide into the first stable pitch of a voiced run whose sound starts, the full-band RMS rising 20 dB, up to 100 ms before it, and the fit also finds its start pitch; a voiced run that starts within 100 ms of the one before joins it when the full-band RMS does not rise 6 dB in the gap, its 10 ms RMS stays within 20 dB of the 20 ms before or after the gap and within 40 dB of the loudest frame of the stem, and the pitch keeps moving after the gap the way it jumped, at 30 cents per millisecond or slower; two stable pitches with a bridged gap between them whose jump goes against the interval by 20 cents or more, or carries more than 60 % of it, join no glide; motion of 35 to 90 ms, over the detected span or the fitted time, counts as too short; a fit of 90 ms or more with p within 5 % of 0.2, with p within 5 % of 5 and an RMS residual above 20 cents, a detected span under 90 ms or over 2.5 times the fitted time, or a start from silence, or with an RMS residual above 40 cents, is no glide; a glide with p within 5 % of 5 reads at low confidence with the reason curve_bound",
    "drops": "f(t) = f_end + df exp(-t / tau) fitted by least squares to the sub-band line from 7 ms to 400 ms after the onset, or to the end of the note; tau by a log grid and golden-section search from 3.04 ms, where exp(-7 ms / tau) = 0.1, to 1 s, f_end and df linear for each tau; a fit with tau under 10 ms, or after a strike whose full-band RMS rises 20 dB, is fitted again on the line with its high-pass at 10 Hz, and the refit counts; df_st = 12 log2((f_end + df) / f_end); onset_s is the first sample after the lowest point of the onset search where the 20 to 200 Hz envelope, averaged over a centred 10 ms, reaches half the peak that follows; a strike whose full-band RMS over the 20 ms after the onset lies more than 40 dB below the loudest 25 ms frame of the stem, or whose 20 to 200 Hz RMS over those 20 ms lies more than 18 dB below the loudest 25 ms frame of that band, is no candidate; a drop with tau under 10 ms needs an envelope that takes 30 ms or less from 10 to 90 % of its peak; a drop with tau under 10 ms, one that starts at 200 Hz or above, or one whose envelope takes over 30 ms from 10 to 90 % of its peak needs the full-band RMS over the 20 ms after the onset 6 dB or more above the 20 ms that end 25 ms before it; residual is the RMS of the fit's error, averaged over half a period of f_end when tau is 10 ms or more and over a full period when tau spans 1.5 periods or more, over the fitted fall from 7 ms on, df exp(-7 ms / tau); a drop counts when df_st is above 2 and at most 36, that fall is above 2 semitones too, tau is above the bound of the search, residual is below 0.15, and f_end lies within 100 cents of a note that starts 150 ms or less before the onset and sounds from 5 tau after the onset, or from the end of the fit span if that comes first, to the end of the fit span; a fit after a 6 dB strike that is no drop is fitted again on the note line, whose low-pass sits at 1.5 times the note's pitch, when that lies under 200 Hz, with its span ending one period of the note before the note line's frequency first falls to 0 Hz, and the refit counts with tau of 10 ms or more and an RMS envelope over its fall, from 7 ms to 5 tau, at most 6 dB below the line the first fit read; an onset before the drop read last has settled, 5 tau after its onset, is the same strike",
    "sub_band_line": "fourth-order Butterworth high-pass at 20 Hz and low-pass at 200 Hz, each forward and backward; the frequency of the analytic signal between consecutive samples, arg(z[n+1] conj(z[n])) fs / 2 pi; a centred median of round(1.4 ms fs) samples, made odd, shortened at the ends; the refit of a drop uses a high-pass at 10 Hz",
    "vibrato": "the voiced f0 frames of a steady span, a voiced run of the track split where two stable pitches lie 150 cents or more apart, without 50 ms at each end, without the frames where a glide's fitted curve lies more than 10 cents from both its pitches and without the settling of a drop, five time constants and at least 100 ms, in cents; start_s and end_s are its first and last frame in audio time; a least-squares line and sine fitted together, at the rate whose sine explains the most power beyond the line, searched from 1 Hz or 1.5 cycles over the span up to 20 Hz in 0.01 Hz steps and refined by golden-section search; extent_raw_ct is that sine's amplitude, half the peak-to-peak swing; extent_ct is extent_raw_ct times extent_factor, which undoes the smoothing of the f0 track at that rate; a vibrato counts at 2.97 to 12.12 Hz, 3 to 12 Hz with 1 % slack, with extent_ct of 10 or more and a share, the power the sine explains over the power left after the line alone, of 0.5 or more, over 2.5 cycles or more"
  }
}
